# Line-ending policy — added 2026-08-21.
#
# WHY. Seven card snippets, packages/watchdog.yaml, configuration.yaml,
# automations.yaml and the two seed scripts had drifted to CRLF and were
# failing .yamllint.yml's `new-lines: unix` rule in CI. This config is edited
# from Windows over a Samba share to the HA host, so any editor that defaults
# to CRLF reintroduces it silently and the build goes red again. Normalising
# in git makes that structurally impossible rather than a thing to remember.
#
# Deliberately scoped to text formats only. CSV is NOT listed: the reporting
# CSVs under www/ and reports/ are append-only data files (see CLAUDE.md
# "NEVER overwrite/truncate CSV files"), and renormalising them on checkout
# would rewrite data this repo treats as immutable.
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sql   text eol=lf

# CSV: explicitly OPTED OUT of normalisation, not merely omitted.
# 2026-08-24: the comment above said CSV was left off this list so the
# append-only reporting data would not be rewritten on checkout. Omission does
# not do that. An unlisted extension is `text: unspecified`, which falls back to
# core.autocrlf - on this Windows/Samba working copy that is exactly the
# rewrite the comment forbids, and git says so: staging www/energy/*.csv emits
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it" 57 times.
# -text turns the stated intent into an enforced one.
*.csv   -text

# Binary — never touch.
*.db    binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pem   binary
